{"kind":"request","text":"Refuse a Git read token to a key named in a compromised notice\n\nScope: from 057d3269 and 30b0942d, decided in the act this rests on. Today a revoked key can sign `read-token` for up to 300 s after a compromised revocation, and the session it holds can read the new token, which lasts up to 24 hours. Refuse `read-token` and the credential route for a key that a `compromised` notice named.\n\nDone when a scope test on real scopes shows both refusals after the notice arrives, a control turns each red, the docs state what is closed and what stays open (a token already read, and the time before the notice arrives), and the gate passes. Name any new Destination definition pin in the review request. No backward compatibility is needed.\n\nOrder: below the current items. This is hosted code, and I deploy it after it lands.","body":{"conditions":"read-token and the credential route refuse a key named in a compromised notice, under a scope test and controls, with the docs stating what stays open, approved by the checker and landed on main.","target_head":"8f129cdf83c36b059adb0a4fe071da9bb7916fa8","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}